WEBVTT

00:00:05.735 --> 00:00:09.489
Ah! Hyah!

00:00:09.572 --> 00:00:13.409
Choose your last words
carefully, Telmarine.

00:00:14.911 --> 00:00:16.663
You are a mouse.

00:00:16.746 --> 00:00:20.708
(sighs) I was hoping
for something a little more original.

00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:22.919
Pick up your sword.

00:00:24.462 --> 00:00:26.965
Uh... No, thanks.

00:00:27.048 --> 00:00:30.301
Pick it up! I will not
fight an unarmed man.

00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:32.512
Which is why I might live longer

00:00:32.595 --> 00:00:35.348
if I choose not to cross blades
with you, noble mouse.

00:00:35.431 --> 00:00:38.935
I said I would not fight you.
I didn't say I'd let you live!

00:00:39.018 --> 00:00:40.687
Reepicheep!

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.189
- Stay your blade!
- Trufflehunter?

00:00:43.273 --> 00:00:47.026
I trust you have a very good reason
for this untimely interruption.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:51.865
- He doesn't. Go ahead.
- He's the one who blew the horn.

00:00:51.948 --> 00:00:56.035
- What?
- Then let him bring it forward.

00:00:59.247 --> 00:01:02.625
This is the reason we have gathered.

00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:09.340
(Susan) I don't remember this way.

00:01:09.424 --> 00:01:12.302
That's the problem with girls.
You can't carry a map in your heads.

00:01:12.385 --> 00:01:14.679
That's because our heads
have something in them.

00:01:15.763 --> 00:01:19.184
I wish he'd just listen
to the D.L.F. in the first place.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:23.897
- D.L.F.?
- Dear Little Friend.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:27.150
Oh, that's not at all
patronizing, is it?

00:01:30.278 --> 00:01:32.405
I'm not lost.

00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:35.074
No.

00:01:35.158 --> 00:01:38.036
You're just going the wrong way.

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:40.246
You last saw Caspian
at the Shuddering Woods,

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:42.957
and the quickest way there
is to cross at the river Rush.

00:01:43.041 --> 00:01:46.753
But unless I'm mistaken, there's
no crossing in these parts.

00:01:46.836 --> 00:01:49.839
That explains it, then.
You're mistaken.

00:02:12.654 --> 00:02:16.574
You see, over time, water erodes
the earth's soil, carving deeper...

00:02:16.658 --> 00:02:18.284
Oh, shut up.

00:02:18.368 --> 00:02:21.621
- Is there a way down?
- Yeah, falling.

00:02:21.704 --> 00:02:24.624
Well, we weren't lost.

00:02:24.707 --> 00:02:27.669
There's a ford near Beruna.
How do you feel about swimming?

00:02:27.752 --> 00:02:29.963
I'd rather that than walking.

00:02:31.256 --> 00:02:33.174
Aslan?

00:02:33.258 --> 00:02:36.094
It's Aslan!
It's Aslan over there!

00:02:36.177 --> 00:02:38.680
Don't you see? He's right...

00:02:42.809 --> 00:02:44.811
...there.

00:02:44.894 --> 00:02:47.105
Do you see him now?

00:02:48.356 --> 00:02:50.149
I'm not crazy.

00:02:50.233 --> 00:02:53.027
He was there.
He wanted us to follow him.

00:02:56.114 --> 00:02:59.075
I'm sure there are any number
of lions in this wood.

00:02:59.158 --> 00:03:02.245
- Just like that bear.
- I think I know Aslan when I see him.

00:03:03.413 --> 00:03:06.124
Look, I'm not about to jump off a cliff

00:03:06.207 --> 00:03:08.334
after someone who doesn't exist.

00:03:08.418 --> 00:03:10.837
The last time I didn't believe Lucy

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.339
I ended up looking pretty stupid.

00:03:19.262 --> 00:03:21.055
Why wouldn't I have seen him?

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:23.474
Maybe you weren't looking.

00:03:25.518 --> 00:03:26.769
I'm sorry, Lu.

00:03:50.752 --> 00:03:53.379
(shouting)

00:03:53.463 --> 00:03:55.048
Kill him!

00:03:55.131 --> 00:03:58.009
- Telmarine!
- Liar!

00:03:58.092 --> 00:03:59.677
Murderer!

00:03:59.761 --> 00:04:02.555
All this horn proves is they've
stolen yet another thing from us!

00:04:02.638 --> 00:04:05.516
- I didn't steal anything.
- Didn't steal anything?

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.394
Shall we list the things
the Telmarines have taken?

00:04:08.478 --> 00:04:10.104
- Our homes!
- Our land!

00:04:10.188 --> 00:04:12.482
- Our freedom!
- Our lives!

00:04:12.565 --> 00:04:13.733
You stole Narnia!

00:04:13.816 --> 00:04:15.568
You would hold me accountable

00:04:15.651 --> 00:04:17.070
for all the crimes of my people?

00:04:17.153 --> 00:04:18.571
Accountable...

00:04:19.489 --> 00:04:21.032
...and punishable.

00:04:21.115 --> 00:04:24.619
Ha! That is rich coming
from you, dwarf.

00:04:24.702 --> 00:04:28.664
Have you forgotten it was your people
who fought alongside the White Witch?

00:04:28.748 --> 00:04:32.543
And I'd gladly do it again,
if it would rid us of these barbarians.

00:04:32.627 --> 00:04:36.089
Then it's lucky that it is not
in your power to bring her back.

00:04:36.172 --> 00:04:40.593
Or are you suggesting that we ask
this boy to go against Aslan now?

00:04:40.676 --> 00:04:43.971
- (roaring)
- (shouting)

00:04:44.055 --> 00:04:47.642
Some of you may have forgotten,
but we badgers remember well...

00:04:47.725 --> 00:04:52.438
...that Narnia was never right except
when a Son of Adam was king.

00:04:52.522 --> 00:04:55.441
He's a Telmarine! Why would
we want him as our king?

00:04:55.525 --> 00:04:57.360
- (shouting)
- Because I can help you.

00:04:57.443 --> 00:05:00.238
- It's a trick!
- At least hear him out!

00:05:00.321 --> 00:05:03.908
Beyond these woods,
I'm a prince.

00:05:03.991 --> 00:05:07.578
The Telmarine throne
is rightfully mine!

00:05:07.662 --> 00:05:11.916
Help me claim it, and I
can bring peace between us.

00:05:13.251 --> 00:05:17.213
It is true. The time is ripe.

00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:20.633
I watch the skies...

00:05:20.716 --> 00:05:25.304
...for it is mine to watch as it
is yours to remember, badger.

00:05:26.889 --> 00:05:31.894
Tarva, the lord of victory,
and Alambil, the lady of peace,

00:05:31.978 --> 00:05:35.022
have come together
in the high heavens.

00:05:36.232 --> 00:05:40.736
And now here,
a Son of Adam has come forth...

00:05:42.113 --> 00:05:45.158
...to offer us back our freedom.

00:05:45.241 --> 00:05:48.286
Is this possible? Do you really
think there could be peace?

00:05:48.369 --> 00:05:50.997
Do you? I mean, really?

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:56.169
Two days ago, I didn't believe in
the existence of talking animals...

00:05:56.252 --> 00:05:59.046
...or dwarves... or centaurs.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.843
Yet here you are
in strength and numbers

00:06:03.926 --> 00:06:06.971
that we Telmarines
could never have imagined.

00:06:07.054 --> 00:06:12.351
Whether this horn is magic
or not, it brought us together.

00:06:12.435 --> 00:06:15.188
And together,

00:06:15.271 --> 00:06:19.150
we have a chance
to take back what is ours.

00:06:19.233 --> 00:06:24.530
If you will lead us,
then my sons and I...

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.451
...offer you our swords.

00:06:37.919 --> 00:06:42.131
And we offer you our lives,
unreservedly.

00:06:43.799 --> 00:06:47.553
Miraz's army will not
be far behind us, sire.

00:06:47.637 --> 00:06:52.683
If we are to be ready for them, we need
to hurry to find soldiers and weapons.

00:06:55.895 --> 00:06:59.023
I'm sure they will be here soon.

00:07:09.158 --> 00:07:13.704
(man) These ones!
And these ones!

00:07:15.706 --> 00:07:18.417
(man 2) Timber!

00:07:18.501 --> 00:07:21.504
- (man 3) Get back!
- Watch your back!

00:07:22.505 --> 00:07:24.507
(man 4) Look out!

00:07:25.883 --> 00:07:28.427
- Steady, steady!
- Timber!

00:07:33.099 --> 00:07:35.685
(men shouting)

00:07:45.861 --> 00:07:48.948
Perhaps this wasn't the best way
to come after all.

